    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag so the owner response reports `true` once more than 80 owners have already been created for today's business day, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `bulkSignupWarning` field with a setter.\n\n2. **`.../function/owner/BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 Small helper that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business day (`BusinessDay.roll(LocalDate.now())`, matching the existing daily-limit and build logic) and returns `true` when the count exceeds 80.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** and **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 Both responders now inject `OwnerRepository`, compute `BulkSignup.warning(...)`, and set it on the DTO before sending. Setting it in both keeps the flag consistent whether the owner is read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` or returned from the create response.\n\nThe threshold is `> 80` (strictly more than 80), and \"today\" is the server date rolled to a business day \u2014 the same effective date that newly created owners land on and that the `RejectDailyLimit` rule caps, keeping the accumulation path identical to the existing daily rules.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` passes (asserts `bulkSignupWarning` is `false` for a fresh create), and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
